# Technical Documentation: 3D Disease Localization Node & Performance Diagnostics

This document records the deployment process of the native C++ 3D localization node (`disease_locator`) and the diagnostic analysis of the message accumulation (Buffer Bloat) issue encountered during real-time testing.

---

 1. Module Overview
The `disease_locator` package is a native C++ ROS2 node designed to bridge 2D computer vision bounding boxes with physical 3D spatial coordinates using an Astra RGBD camera. 

* **Subscribed Topics:**
  * `/detections` (`vision_msgs/msg/Detection2DArray`): Provides 2D bounding box center pixel coordinates $(u, v)$ from the YOLOv8 inference node.
  * `/camera/depth/image_raw` (`sensor_msgs/msg/Image`): Provides the raw depth matrix mapping pixels to real-world distances.

---

 2. Core Source Code (`locator_node.cpp`)

```cpp
#include <rclcpp/rclcpp.hpp>
#include <sensor_msgs/msg/image.hpp>
#include <vision_msgs/msg/detection2_d_array.hpp>
#include <cv_bridge/cv_bridge.h>

class DiseaseLocator : public rclcpp::Node {
public:
    DiseaseLocator() : Node("disease_locator_node") {
        depth_sub_ = this->create_subscription<sensor_msgs::msg::Image>(
            "/camera/depth/image_raw", rclcpp::SensorDataQoS(),
            std::bind(&DiseaseLocator::depth_callback, this, std::placeholders::_1));

        detect_sub_ = this->create_subscription<vision_msgs::msg::Detection2DArray>(
            "/detections", 10,
            std::bind(&DiseaseLocator::detect_callback, this, std::placeholders::_1));

        RCLCPP_INFO(this->get_logger(), "Disease Locator Node Initialized! Awaiting data...");
    }

private:
    rclcpp::Subscription<sensor_msgs::msg::Image>::SharedPtr depth_sub_;
    rclcpp::Subscription<vision_msgs::msg::Detection2DArray>::SharedPtr detect_sub_;
    cv_bridge::CvImagePtr cv_depth_ptr_;

    void depth_callback(const sensor_msgs::msg::Image::SharedPtr msg) {
        try {
            cv_depth_ptr_ = cv_bridge::toCvCopy(msg, msg->encoding);
        } catch (cv_bridge::Exception& e) {
            RCLCPP_ERROR(this->get_logger(), "cv_bridge exception: %s", e.what());
        }
    }

    void detect_callback(const vision_msgs::msg::Detection2DArray::SharedPtr msg) {
        if (!cv_depth_ptr_) return; 

        for (const auto& detection : msg->detections) {
            int u = static_cast<int>(detection.bbox.center.position.x);
            int v = static_cast<int>(detection.bbox.center.position.y);

            if (u >= 0 && u < cv_depth_ptr_->image.cols && v >= 0 && v < cv_depth_ptr_->image.rows) {
                float depth_val = 0.0;
                
                if (cv_depth_ptr_->image.type() == CV_16UC1) {
                    depth_val = cv_depth_ptr_->image.at<uint16_t>(v, u) / 1000.0; 
                } else if (cv_depth_ptr_->image.type() == CV_32FC1) {
                    depth_val = cv_depth_ptr_->image.at<float>(v, u);
                }

                if (depth_val > 0.0) {
                    RCLCPP_INFO(this->get_logger(), 
                        "TARGET LOCKED | Pixel (x:%d, y:%d) -> Physical Distance Z: %.3f meters", 
                        u, v, depth_val);
                }
            }
        }
    }
};

int main(int argc, char** argv) {
    rclcpp::init(argc, argv);
    rclcpp::spin(std::make_shared<DiseaseLocator>());
    rclcpp::shutdown();
    return 0;
}

